// Figure 3.1 — Agile Scrum development cycle (two-week sprints)
// Eraser: New diagram > Flow chart, paste this code.
direction right

Product backlog [shape: document, icon: list, color: gray]
Sprint planning [shape: oval, icon: calendar, color: blue]
Sprint backlog [shape: document, icon: clipboard, color: gray]

Two-week sprint [color: blue] {
  Develop [icon: code]
  Test [icon: check-circle]
  Daily review of progress [icon: refresh-cw]
}

Working increment [shape: rectangle, icon: package, color: green]
Sprint review with supervisor [shape: oval, icon: users, color: orange]
Sprint retrospective [shape: oval, icon: rotate-ccw, color: purple]

Product backlog > Sprint planning: prioritise must / should / could
Sprint planning > Sprint backlog
Sprint backlog > Develop
Develop > Test
Test > Daily review of progress
Daily review of progress > Develop: next task
Test > Working increment
Working increment > Sprint review with supervisor: demonstrate
Sprint review with supervisor > Sprint retrospective
Sprint retrospective > Product backlog: adjust plan and requirements
